triage: revise_rules: The game is built correctly, but a thoughtless policy (always take the last offered option, which is the biggest multi-card play or bomb) wins 77-90% of games. The rules make dumping the largest play dominant: a triple or run lead is almost never answerable, so shedding three cards at a time beats any real decision.
